    url          = {https://doi.org/10.1145/3618260.3664271},
    abstract     = {
        Turing-complete blockchain protocols approximate the idealized abstraction of a "computer
        in the sky" that is open access, runs in plain view, and, in effect, has no owner or
        operator. This technology can, among other things, enable stronger notions of ownership of
        digital possessions than we have ever had before. Building the computer in the sky is hard
        (and scientifically fascinating). In this talk I'll highlight some of my recent research on
