    abstract     = {
        This article explores the tokenization of the artwork Carnaval de Binche (1924) by James
        Ensor through a collaboration between the Rubey platform and the Royal Museum of Fine Arts
        Antwerp. Investors can purchase blockchain-registered Art Security Tokens and become
        co-owners of the artwork, which remains on public display in the museum for ten years.
